A||||8||V8Dreamer||NTB trying to rip me off!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||V8Dreamer||09-06-2001||09:52 PM||||Well, I took my newly lowered GT to NTB for a 4-wheel alignment yesterday.....Alignment guy put the thing on the lift (which took 3 boards to avoid scraping)  and after about 5 minutes, he told me that because it was too low he couldn't even get a toe reading, so I had to remove the airdam for him.  After that he adjusted the toe and lowered the lift and got in the car(now this is supposed to be a 4-wheel alignment mind you)  and I asked him if he was sure he didn't need to make any adjustments to the rear since the rear camber WAS about 8 degrees off.  His answer was that "We only do front toe on fieros cause they rust up too bad."  Anyway, after a little discussion with the manager, I got the toe adjusted....then he was ready to pull it off the lift again....after an argument with the manager, and him insisting that camber adjustment wasn't included and me saying BS!  They finally adjusted the camber.  All in all, it got done, it just took 3 hours and a lot of arguing....sorry for rambling, I just wanted to let someone know about that one....<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||09-06-2001||10:04 PM||||Your first mistake was not taking your car to the dealer. Second was going to NTB.<P>I've heard stories about NTB. I buy tires from them, but my car never goes there. They mount tires on the rims, I take teh wheels home and put them on my car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BV MotorSports||09-07-2001||02:00 PM||||About a yr ago I had nothing but good things to say about NTB. I have the life time alignment on my Fiero. After the car setting for a yr I decided to start driving her again. I took her up to NTB and they refused to honor my Life time alignment cause I didnt have the card any more. I showed them 4 of my last alignment reciepts and he still refused. Looking into the computer it showed all 15(!) of my alignments where free~!<BR>After me getting very loud and rude in front of a lot of customers he agreed to do it for free. I siad not free, just honor the life time alignment I purchased. He then said dont expect it next time. Oh boy! I wont repeat what I then said but lets just say it wasnt nice. they also tried to get out of adjusting the caster on the car. Its not adjustible on a fiero. Oh but it is! You just dont want to do it. Besides moron...I have the Moog problem solver ball joints. <BR>Its getting really hard to find a good shop these days.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-07-2001||03:55 PM||||I call 'em NAB.<BR>National Assault & Battery. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Dreamer||09-07-2001||04:22 PM||||Well, at least I'm not the only one.....I definately won't go back to say the least.  I just found out about a good shop that doesn't b*tch about doing Fieros and does the camber adjustments too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks<BR>Ryan ||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||09-07-2001||06:47 PM||||NTB - we all have good stories.  Mine last week. Due to circumstances, my son-in-law takes my other Pontiac for one tire.  Bill brought to me was $164 which included an alignment (front only for $40.00).  Yesterday, I take car to Discount.  Tire was $52.16.  Alignment not needed.  'Nough said!||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||09-07-2001||08:23 PM||||I'll buy tires there... They take my sears card and they have good tires at decent prices. I do watch them, and any other place, like a hawk. One time when I did the Fiero there they almost lifted on the pipes...<P>The majority of tire places bite. It's not unique to NTB. If you think they are bad try Sears service centers. I've never seen them do anything without some kind of major screwup. Sears is about the worst place on earth to shop at. The only reason I keep the card is that I can get nearly anything from them in a cash crunch. (I do like our sears appliance clearance center... got the dryer there. payed about half-2/3 the normal price.)<P>When my water pump quit, I took it to pep boys. I had to work. They got it done by 5. The ones around here have been pretty decent. I haven't had any trouble with the new pump an it's been at least 2 years now. nealry all pep boys people are ASE's.||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnF||09-07-2001||08:28 PM||||Guess I've been really lucky!  All my "real" mechanic work is done by a privately owned garage staffed exclusively with ASE types who labor at about 2/3 the going GM rate.  The owner has taken personal responsibility of my baby and has always treated it with respect.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fformula88||09-07-2001||11:12 PM||||NTB is owned by Sears... its really a Sears service dept. by another name.<P>This doesn't mean they are bad of course... depends on who they have working for them and how well they are managed.<P>Locally we have a tire place called "Dunn Tire".  They are just a local company, but are absolutely awesome with tire/alignment service.  They ran all the NTB's around Buffalo out of business!<P>I find the best place for an alignment is the corner mechanic who has the equipment to do it.  Dealers aren't too good IMO... they are usually more expensive and aren't as concerned about doing a "quality" job.<P>I had a Pontiac Dealer intentionally sabotage some parts on my Fiero to get some extra repair work!  I just don't trust 'em!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
